Cairnfold includes these human motion recordings, captured by the CMU Graphics Lab
with a Vicon system, as part of the game, not as a standalone motion product. They
are not relicensed under Cairnfold's MIT/Apache licenses. The original files are in
third_party/cmu/. scripts/mocap.gd converts them, authoring no rotations or
keyframes:

- Subject 141, trial 16, "Wave Hello", into head-relative hand aim transforms at
  its original 120 Hz for game/animations/wave.tres; the avatar uses the same hand
  targets as VR tracking.
- Single frames of subjects 140, 82 and 14 into body poses for
  game/animations/poses.json: each bone's turn from the recording's T-pose, as
  captured; the side pose is also kept mirrored left for right.
  - Subject 140, trial 8, "Get Up From Ground Laying on Back", frame 1: on the back.
  - Subject 140, trial 3, "Get Up Laying on Side", frame 1: on the side.
  - Subject 140, trial 1, "Get Up Face Down", frame 1: on the front.
  - Subject 82, trial 5, "sitting on ground relaxing", frames 1 (hands forward)
    and 2197 (leaning back on the hands).
  - Subject 14, trial 31, "sit on stepstool, stand up", frame 721: on a ledge.

